+// network map's version of that peer, **in place**.
+//
+// Why in place: the WireGuard device pins the endpoint object it was given when
+// the peer was created (lazily, via [Conn.ParseEndpoint]) and never roams to a
+// different object. Replacing the object (delete + create) therefore leaves
+// the device sending handshake responses and data through an orphaned endpoint
